# Budgety Design System

## Source of truth

Stitch project [9083140746767418409](https://stitch.withgoogle.com/projects/9083140746767418409) — assets in `stitch-assets/`, icons in `src/components/icons/` + `public/icons/stitch/`. User screenshots (Home / Transaction / Analytics / Profile / Add sheet) drive the mobile shell.

## Stack

- **Next.js App Router** + React 19
- **Tailwind CSS** for layout, spacing, color utilities (`darkMode: "class"`)
- Shared UI: `@common/*`, `@components/icons`, `@components/mobile`, `@components/screens`

## Light / dark themes

| Mode | Visual system | Tokens |
| ---- | ------------- | ------ |
| Light | Stitch **Luminous Precision** | `:root` in `globals.css`, `STITCH_COLORS` |
| Dark | Stitch **Obsidian Flux** surfaces + Budgety purple brand | `html.dark` in `globals.css`, `STITCH_DARK_COLORS` |

### Strategy

- Tailwind `darkMode: "class"` — toggle via `html.dark` (not `prefers-color-scheme` alone).
- Preference: `light` | `dark` | `system`, stored under **`budgety.theme`** (`THEME_STORAGE_KEY` in `src/lib/theme.ts`).
- `ThemeProvider` (`src/components/providers/ThemeProvider.tsx`) reads/writes preference, resolves system, applies `class` + `colorScheme` + `data-theme`.
- FOUC script in `src/app/layout.tsx` applies the class before paint.
- UI: `ThemeToggle` on Profile → Appearance; compact toggle on desktop `TopBar`.
- Prefer semantic tokens (`bg-surface`, `bg-card`, `text-brand-deep`, `text-on-surface-variant`, `border-outline-variant`) over raw hex.
- Charts: use `CHART_THEME_COLORS` from `@/lib/theme` (CSS vars) so strokes/fills follow the active theme.
- `globals.css` remaps common light-only utilities (`bg-white`, gray text/borders) under `html.dark` for legacy screens.

Do not use `lucide-react` or `@mui/icons-material`. Icons are Stitch Material Symbol SVGs from `@components/icons`.

